Source landscape: Germany in 2023 yields a mixed but fairly dense documentary field for Chapter 3B, with the most useful leads coming from German official crime/violence statistics, federal ministry releases, UN review documents, Council of Europe / ECRI material, Amnesty / HRW / ECRE submissions, and German court decisions on protests and assembly bans. The strongest clusters are protest policing, police accountability, hate crime, domestic and gender-based violence, refugee / asylum security, and independent oversight. A few academic and legal sources are paywalled or likely access-limited, but still worth keeping as candidates.

